349
00:20:30,220 --> 00:20:34,460
that music other than the human voice that

350
00:20:34,460 --> 00:20:36,820
was all that was needed in the church

351
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:40,480
service and so it was provided that the organ be

352
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:45,280
used for a month and if there was any serious

353
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:50,220
objection to it then it was to be removed. One

354
00:20:50,220 --> 00:20:56,000
of the things that is interesting about

355
00:20:56,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Dr. Marshall was that he loved books and when

356
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:05,040
you visit his monument in the cemetery you'll

357
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:07,980
find that it has an open book that's the only

358
00:21:07,980 --> 00:21:15,040
visible marking other than the information as

359
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:19,020
to his birth and death on his tombstone.

360
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:24,580
And interesting enough, when I found the will,

361
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:27,960
he provides in here for the division of his

362
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:28,400
library

363
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:31,080
among various members of his family

364
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:35,180
