366
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:41,000
And then he goes on to say that whatever is left

367
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,020
should be disposed of.

368
00:21:43,780 --> 00:21:47,100
So heavens knows where all of this library is at

369
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:49,300
the present time, but it was a considerable

370
00:21:49,300 --> 00:21:51,620
number of books.

371
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:51,933
And books in those days were extremely expensive

372
00:21:51,933 --> 00:21:52,200
and valuable.

373
00:21:55,000 --> 00:22:01,640
So, to have an extensive library such as that

374
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:03,560
was quite a mark of distinction.

375
00:22:05,180 --> 00:22:08,380
And again, as I said, he was an expert linguist.

376
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:14,880
He spoke Hebrew and Latin fluently, and I guess

377
00:22:14,880 --> 00:22:16,820
he was a compulsive student.

378
00:22:16,820 --> 00:22:23,140
He studied all his life and was very interested

379
00:22:23,140 --> 00:22:25,620
in furthering the cause of education.

380
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:32,400
I think he lived in a very tragic period.

381
00:22:32,640 --> 00:22:34,780
If you looked at him, you noticed that he

382
00:22:34,780 --> 00:22:36,100
