383
00:22:36,140 --> 00:22:38,120
He wasn't well most of his life.

384
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:41,780
I think probably what his problem was that he

385
00:22:41,780 --> 00:22:42,580
had an ulcer.

386
00:22:42,700 --> 00:22:44,460
I should have Jane here.

387
00:22:44,460 --> 00:22:46,860
I said, he suffered from dyspepsia.

388
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:49,100
Doesn't that sound like an ulcer to you?

389
00:22:50,620 --> 00:22:55,340
And I pulled up his old trunk there.

390
00:22:55,980 --> 00:22:57,920
That was one of the things that was in John

391
00:22:57,920 --> 00:22:58,940
McCabe's barn.

392
00:22:59,900 --> 00:23:04,160
And I brought it back because the trunk sort of,

393
00:23:05,220 --> 00:23:08,120
I keep thinking to myself that old trunk

394
00:23:08,120 --> 00:23:09,060
could only speak

395
00:23:09,060 --> 00:23:14,560
the many things that it could possibly tell us.

396
00:23:14,740 --> 00:23:22,420
In fact, I wrote down some of the places that I

397
00:23:22,420 --> 00:23:26,520
know he did travel. And think in terms of travel

398
00:23:26,520 --> 00:23:32,180
in the period that he lived. I just found

399
00:23:32,180 --> 00:23:32,900
recently

400
00:23:32,900 --> 00:23:36,360
that on my mother's side, my great-grandfather

401
00:23:36,360 --> 00:23:41,680
was a canal boat captain, and he ran the canal

402
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:46,240
boats from Johnstown to Pittsburgh. So it struck

403
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:50,060
me, isn't it ironic, I'm sure that he probably

404
00:23:50,060 --> 00:23:50,560
had

405
00:23:51,460 --> 00:23:54,100
drawn one of the canal boats that...

406
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:57,180
Reverend Marshall traveled because he traveled

407
00:23:57,180 --> 00:24:00,700
extensively to the eastern part of the state,

408
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:05,060
and because of his health, in the summer of

409
00:24:05,060 --> 00:24:10,900
1851, he, along with Thomas Cadoux, who was an

