508
00:29:30,850 --> 00:29:32,830
There were 7,000 present.

509
00:29:33,010 --> 00:29:35,650
I got a good seat in front part of the balcony

510
00:29:35,650 --> 00:29:37,030
and heard her very distinctly,

511
00:29:37,550 --> 00:29:39,490
and all for $1.

512
00:29:40,570 --> 00:29:43,490
Which you love to hear Jenny Lind for $1.

513
00:29:43,490 --> 00:29:46,330
And in an age when you're paying $1 for

514
00:29:46,330 --> 00:29:50,010
entertainment with 25 cents or 50 cents for your

515
00:29:50,010 --> 00:29:53,430
truck, they really were asking a bit.

516
00:29:53,590 --> 00:29:57,210
It's basically about a dollar today, so that was

517
00:29:57,210 --> 00:29:57,710
expensive.

518
00:29:58,050 --> 00:29:58,310
Yes.

519
00:29:58,310 --> 00:30:00,430
Of course, maybe they were hauling it 50 miles.

520
00:30:00,530 --> 00:30:04,510
Well, he doesn't indicate that.

521
00:30:04,890 --> 00:30:08,750
Then there's one cute little thing here at the

522
00:30:08,750 --> 00:30:09,490
end. He said,

523
00:30:12,930 --> 00:30:15,930
Tomorrow we sail, the Lord willing. Our cabin is

524
00:30:15,930 --> 00:30:18,950
not what it was represented to be. And you may

525
00:30:18,950 --> 00:30:22,050
tell Alex Ringsoe if you see him. I gather Alex

526
00:30:22,050 --> 00:30:24,610
Ringsoe wasn't at the reservation.

527
00:30:27,810 --> 00:30:31,570
And so he says write to me direct to Brown,

528
00:30:31,570 --> 00:30:34,010
Shipley and Company, Liverpool, England and tell

529
00:30:34,010 --> 00:30:36,630
me all the news my love to sister phoebe

530
00:30:36,630 --> 00:30:40,350
remember me in your prayers and a delightful

531
00:30:40,350 --> 00:30:41,330
letter from

532
00:30:41,330 --> 00:30:43,070
the other correspondence you've read from that

533
00:30:43,070 --> 00:30:46,150
period of time that he seems very direct and

534
00:30:46,150 --> 00:30:50,110
almost hardship points in letters which

535
00:30:50,110 --> 00:30:50,270
Thank you.
